Iranian chart extension (US-502), English chart tree: template accounts
added to the Universal Chart of Accounts for HesabYar. They are created
for a company either by a fresh install_chart, or by update_chart on an
existing company (the Adapter Test company picks them up that way).

This follows the Tryton-native per-language chart pattern (see
account_asset/account_chart_en.xml): the account module ships one chart
tree per language (account_chart_en.xml etc., ids suffixed _en), and a
chart extension ships one file per language it supports, attaching to
that language's tree. HesabYar ships only the English file: the dev DB
(and the product's Tryton server) runs with language 'en', so the
English tree is the one installed. On a database without English, this
file is skipped and the accounts simply do not exist (graceful
degradation, not a failure). Names are English, consistent with the
rest of the English chart; the Persian labels live in the HesabYar
dashboard, which maps account codes to Persian names in its own UI.

Design notes:
- 1.2.4 / 1.2.5 / 2.1.5 mirror the existing 1.2.1 / 2.1.1 leaves:
  party_required + reconcile, under the same parents.
- 1.1.5 / 1.2.6 / 1.2.7 / 2.1.6 are the cash-box accounts (US-516):
  1.1.5 is the petty-cash (تنخواه) account, 1.2.6 the cash
  shortage/overage account (variance policy a), 1.2.7 / 2.1.6 the
  temporary-debtor / miscellaneous-creditor accounts (variance
  policy b). All four are party_required=False: the cashier is
  named in the counting session and the signed minutes, not as a
  Tryton party. None is reconciled: a shortage/overage journal is
  closed at period end (policy a) or settled within 24h (policy b)
  by its own journal, never by reconciling move lines.
- The 7.x memorandum groups carry NO type: Tryton refuses move lines
  on typeless accounts (account.move.Line.check_account), so a group
  without a type is unpostable by construction, that is exactly how
  the universal chart's own groups (1.2.0, 2.1.0) work. Only the
  leaves carry the off-balance type, and they are party_required so
  cheque journals post per party.
- The 7.2.x contra accounts mirror the 7.1.x accounts one-for-one:
  every memorandum debit has its contra credit, so the memorandum
  section always nets to zero (Iranian انتظامی bookkeeping).
- 1.2.9 is the bounced-cheque account (US-530): Bounced Cheques
  (چک‌های برگشتی / مطالبات غیرجاری) — the bounce destination when
  the installation chooses it over Accounts Receivable (§5 §9.1
  #2; default stays Accounts Receivable, see docs/cheque-decisions.md).
  party_required + reconcile, like the other receivables leaves.
- 1.1.6 / 1.2.8 / 5.2.4 are the settlement accounts (US-522):
  1.2.8 is the gateway-receivable account (party_required +
  reconcile: one receivable per gateway party, dunning/aging per
  tranche line); 1.1.6 is the gateway clearing account (money in
  transit between the gateway payout and the bank deposit — NOT
  party_required, like the cash accounts, but reconcile=True so the
  bank-statement flow can reconcile the clearing legs later; the
  clearing module only reconciles clearing lines that sum to zero,
  so a one-sided clearing leg never reconciles by accident);
  5.2.4 is the gateway-fee expense (SG&A). The fee VAT goes to the
  universal chart's 6.3.6 Non-Deductible VAT while
  fee_vat_claimable=false (phased design §3.6: claimable only with
  an official gateway invoice/Moadian record); no new account is
  needed for it.
-->
